  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The root cause of the event was attributed to overconfidence of the work team during validation activities. The team incorrectly assumed the work planning and clearance processes had established conditions for conducting work activities safely...the team performed an inadequate clearance boundary verification using a marked-up copy of the site electrical distribution one-line drawing, which shows only the power feeds into the switchgear, not the cross-ties between the switchgear cubicles...contrary to a station procedure, the work team had utilized an organizationally accepted behavior that performing Live-Dead-Live checks is not required when there is confidence that energy is not present.",
    "cause_code": "A",
    "category": "Personnel Error",
    "theme": "Worker overconfidence / inadequate clearance boundary verification leading to inadvertent contact with energized switchgear",
    "provisional": false
  },
